  "result": "`slugify(text)` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes with all 10 tests (the 2 existing ones plus 8 new).\n\n- **Order of steps:** it turns `đ`/`Đ` into `d` first, since those letters don't decompose into a base letter plus accent. It then strips diacritics and lowercases. Every run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen, and leading and trailing hyphens are trimmed.\n- **50-character limit:** it cuts at 50 characters, then removes any trailing hyphen the cut left behind.\n- **Tests:** the new ones are in `test/strings.test.js`. They cover:\n  - basic hyphenation\n  - Vietnamese text\n  - other Latin accents\n  - runs of symbols\n  - trimming\n  - empty and symbol-only input\n  - truncation at 50 characters\n  - a cut that would land on a hyphen\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
